"financial_summary":["Sweetgreen, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.4B market cap on $679M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -56% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $119M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -15.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -7332.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (25.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 28% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6078431372549015},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 311% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (90% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $4.3M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Sweetgreen (NYSE:SG) Announces Earnings Results, Hits Expectations","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/sweetgreen-nysesg-announces-earnings-results-hits-expectations.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794013006.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Here's What Key Metrics Tell Us About Sweetgreen (SG) Q3 Earnings","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025907/here-s-what-key-metrics-tell-us-about-sweetgreen-sg-q3-earnings?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm-3025907","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793988001.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Oppenheimer Issues Positive Forecast for Sweetgreen (NYSE:SG) Stock Price","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/oppenheimer-issues-positive-forecast-for-sweetgreen-nysesg-stock-price.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793986608.0,"origin":"tiingo","senti